WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.240
Hello everybody, my name is Markiplier and welcome to Doom.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.160
Now, Doom is very important to me.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:10.200
Not necessarily this game, but what it represents in PC gaming.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:15.400
Because the original Doom is one of the first games that I EVER played.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.900
When my dad first introduced me to computers

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:19.540
and gaming in general,

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:21.580
this was the first game that I touched

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:24.360
and it's the first game that I sat down and played

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.360
over and over and over again

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:27.780
and I played the Demo version,

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.260
and then he got me the full game,

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:33.000
and it was just an absolute awesome time.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.480
And I'm gonna play it on 'Ultra-Violence'

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.520
just because I'm actually pretty decent

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:37.500
at first-person shooters

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.720
and I want to give myself some kind of a challenge.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:42.820
There's obviously 'Nightmare' and 'Ultra-Nightmare' afterwards.

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:44.920
Now, when I look at games like this

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:48.160
I intentionally don't go into details

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:49.440
about what the game is about,

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.480
so this might not be-

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:52.200
[Game narration begins]

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:52.700
oo!

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:02.240
Rip and tear!

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:04.540
RIP AND TEAR!!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.120
I love it, I LOVE IT!

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:10.060
That might be a reference to the Doom-

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:10.760
Oh, hello!

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:11.760
What is that?

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:12.800
Hi!

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:14.220
Ohh.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:17.400
Seems like, seems like a scene from Outlast.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.680
Oh hi, could you back away a little bit?

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:20.680
Ohhhh, hi.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:25.120
Oh my god!

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.200
[Sadistic laughter]

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:29.300
Oh, man.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:30.840
Oh! Am I playing right now?

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:31.700
I'm playing RIGHT now!

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:33.100
Holy shit, that's what I like,

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:34.340
getting right into the action!

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:35.620
Okay, so-

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:37.080
Oh hello, didn't see you there.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:39.540
Okay, so I played just a test map

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:41.100
on the, ah, the SnapMaps

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.700
which is the customizable maps that you guys

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:45.140
in the community can make.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:47.400
But the thing about this game is,

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.840
and what scared me in the original was that

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:53.220
it's very inspired by the hellish nature of hell

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:54.840
and all that that represents.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.360
But in reality,

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:01.420
I'm not entirely sure how much-- hello -- that translates to this one.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:02.560
Who are you?

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:04.160
Ohhh, man.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:07.000
This is like a combination of technology

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.480
and like, like satanic things

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:11.480
and it's kinda cool, because-

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:12.540
(We've got to contain this...)

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:13.160
Oh, okay.

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:14.960
We have to...

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:17.100
contain me?

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:20.400
Are you talking about me? Because I was on that table by myself.

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:21.620
Okay. So-

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:22.500
Ohhhh.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:23.860
Hello!

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:26.440
[Laughs] It's so cool!

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:27.980
I'm sorry, I'm nerding out.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:30.080
I get so jazzed up about these-

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:30.660
Hello...

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:38.620
[Cool, slightly demonic-sounding effects]

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:39.780
